   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Light",
     "md": "**Light** comes from **sources** such as the Sun, a fire and a lamp. It travels in **straight lines**. **Transparent** materials let light through (clear glass), **translucent** ones let some through (frosted glass) and **opaque** ones let none through (wood, metal). A **shadow** forms when an opaque object blocks the light."
