   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Magnets",
     "md": "A **magnet** attracts objects made of **iron or steel** (nails, pins). It does not attract wood, plastic, glass or copper. Every magnet has two **poles**, north and south. **Unlike poles attract** (N and S), **like poles repel** (N and N, or S and S). A magnet is strongest at its poles."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "A simple circuit",
     "md": "A bulb lights when it is part of a **closed circuit**: a **cell**, **wires**, a **bulb** and a **switch** joined in a loop. If there is a gap (the switch is open) or a broken wire, the circuit is open and the bulb does not light. **Conductors** (copper, iron) let electricity pass; **insulators** (plastic, rubber, wood) do not."
    },
